From: Joel Winarske <joel.winarske@linux.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Wait for the scheduler before destroying a UserSecureManager

Every UserSecureManager shares one scheduler.  A task holds a future handle
into its manager's future_api_ until the scheduler destroys the task, which
is after the task has run.  The destructor waited for a running task and then
destroyed future_api_, while the scheduler thread was still dropping the
task.  FutureHandle's destructor read api_, future_api_'s cleanup cleared it,
and the handle called ReleaseFuture through null.

With one manager the destructor deletes the scheduler, which joins its thread
first.  With two, as when a second App has an Auth, the scheduler stays and
nothing waits.

Schedule one more task and wait for it.  Tasks run in the order scheduled and
each is destroyed before the next is taken, so every earlier one is gone.

Upstream: https://github.com/firebase/firebase-cpp-sdk/issues/1969

---
 app/src/secure/user_secure_manager.cc |   22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/app/src/secure/user_secure_manager.cc b/app/src/secure/user_secure_manager.cc
index 0f24c53..a26c827 100644
--- a/app/src/secure/user_secure_manager.cc
+++ b/app/src/secure/user_secure_manager.cc
@@ -15,12 +15,14 @@
 #include "app/src/secure/user_secure_manager.h"
 
 #include <cstdint>
+#include <memory>
 #include <utility>
 
 #include "app/src/base64.h"
 #include "app/src/callback.h"
 #include "app/src/include/firebase/internal/platform.h"
 #include "app/src/secure/user_secure_internal.h"
+#include "app/src/semaphore.h"
 
 // Only build this implementation on desktop. If building for iOS or Android,
 // omit it entirely. Until we implement UserSecureInternal for those platforms,
@@ -53,6 +55,20 @@ namespace secure {
 
 using callback::NewCallback;
 
+namespace {
+
+// Returns once the scheduler has run and destroyed every task queued before
+// this call. Tasks are run in the order they were scheduled, and each is
+// destroyed before the next is taken.
+void WaitForScheduler(scheduler::Scheduler* scheduler) {
+  auto reached = std::make_shared<Semaphore>(0);
+  scheduler->Schedule(NewCallback(
+      [](std::shared_ptr<Semaphore> done) { done->Post(); }, reached));
+  reached->Wait();
+}
+
+}  // namespace
+
 Mutex* UserSecureManager::s_scheduler_mutex_ = new Mutex();
 scheduler::Scheduler* UserSecureManager::s_scheduler_;
 int32_t UserSecureManager::s_scheduler_ref_count_;
@@ -76,6 +92,12 @@ UserSecureManager::~UserSecureManager() {
   // Clear safe reference immediately so that scheduled callback can skip
   // executing code which requires reference to this.
   safe_this_.ClearReference();
+  // The scheduler is shared, and outlives this manager when another one is
+  // using it. A task holds a future handle into future_api_ until the
+  // scheduler destroys the task, which is after the task has run and released
+  // the reference above. Destroying future_api_ meanwhile races the handle's
+  // destructor, so wait for the scheduler to let go of the tasks first.
+  WaitForScheduler(s_scheduler_);
   DestroyScheduler();
 }
 
